# The star catalog (source lines 1371-1866), the sky of the Expensive
# Planetarium (heavens.runs). Stars by Peter Samson for Spacewar 2b. It is
# data on the tape, as the outlines are; conceptually it is an asset (AEMS).
#
# Each star is two words, one slot each: its x, then its y. The source
# writes a star `mark X, Y`: X is 0..8192 along the whole band of sky and Y
# is -512..+512 in display points. The word holds 8192 - X, so stars of
# increasing X run right to left, and Y in the word's high bits, where the
# display reads it (`repeat 8, Y=Y+Y`). Each star's comment is its catalog
# number, constellation and name. The four magnitudes lie one after the
# other: the first from slot 0 (1j), the second from 022 (2j), the third
# from 044 (3j) and the fourth from 0306 (4j), up to 01652.
